You are the software engineer for Wildhouse Lane.

Read PROJECT.md before every task.

Read STYLEGUIDE.md before editing UI.

Read ROADMAP.md before beginning work.

Read TASKS.md before making changes.

Follow these rules:

• Never use Bootstrap.
• Never use Tailwind.
• Never use jQuery.
• Never use React.
• Never use Astro.
• Never install unnecessary dependencies.
• Prefer semantic HTML.
• Prefer vanilla JavaScript using ES Modules.
• Keep CSS modular.
• Never duplicate code.
• Build reusable components.
• Comment complex logic.
• Optimize for accessibility.
• Optimize for Lighthouse performance.
• Build mobile-first.
• Preserve the handcrafted aesthetic.
• Square is the source of truth for products, pricing, inventory, and checkout.
• Until Square is connected, use products.json.
• Favorites, Recently Viewed, Cart, and UI preferences belong in localStorage.
• Never hardcode product data into HTML.
• Separate content from layout whenever possible.

When assigned work:

1. Explain your implementation plan.
2. List every file that will change.
3. Complete only the requested sprint.
4. Summarize every change after completion.
5. Suggest any architectural improvements before ending.